# Tests are checked by the same rules as the rest of the code (the settings
# in the repository's .clang-tidy apply here too), with one exception: the
# Clang Static Analyzer is left out.
#
# The analyzer explores the paths a function can take, and a test written
# with GoogleTest's macros has a great many: every EXPECT_ is a branch with a
# message stream behind it. Analysing the tests took 85% of the whole
# clang-tidy run (20 to 40 seconds for a single test file, against about one
# second without it). What it looks for there, the tests already expose by
# being run under the address and undefined-behaviour sanitizers. For the
# code under test, which has paths no test takes, it stays on.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: '-clang-analyzer-*'
